WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Count the links in almost any food chain.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.970
You rarely get past 4 or 5 levels.

3
00:00:06.020 --> 00:00:10.030
And at the very top, the
predators are few and far between.

4
00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:14.920
The same field feeds far more people when
it grows crops than when it grazes animals

5
00:00:14.970 --> 00:00:15.980
for meat.

6
00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.880
So why are top predators so rare, and why
does eating lower in a food chain feed

7
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:22.300
more people?

8
00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:25.520
In this mission, you'll climb
a staircase of feeding levels,

9
00:00:25.570 --> 00:00:27.950
from plants to top predators.

10
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:33.300
Then you'll weigh up why food chains
so rarely grow past 4 or 5 levels.

11
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.810
Your mission: explain why
top predators are rare,

12
00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:39.810
and why eating lower in a
chain feeds more people.
